    termsOfUseLiabilityTitle: "9. Liability Limitations",
    termsOfUseLiabilityContent:
      "Disputes: Disputes are first sought to be resolved internally through the platform's dispute resolution mechanism. If resolution is not possible, the dispute is referred to Omani courts or arbitration as agreed by the parties, and Omani law applies.\nLimitation: The platform is not responsible for service errors; the maximum compensation is the service value.\nTermination: We have the right to terminate accounts for violations (such as fraud).",
    termsOfUseIndemnityTitle: "10. Indemnity",
    termsOfUseIndemnityContent:
      "Each user is obligated to indemnify the platform for any claims resulting from breach of terms or misuse of the service or breach of third-party rights.",
    termsOfUseAccountTerminationTitle: "11. Account Termination",
    termsOfUseAccountTerminationContent:
      "The platform has the right to suspend or terminate accounts upon material breach of terms or suspicion of fraudulent behavior, with notice and/or refund procedures for deposited funds according to the refund policy.",
    termsOfUseGoverningLawTitle: "12. Governing Law",
    termsOfUseGoverningLawContent:
      "These terms are governed by the laws of the Sultanate of Oman. For complaints, contact customer support or the Consumer Protection Authority.",
    termsOfUseModificationsTitle: "13. Modifications",
    termsOfUseModificationsContent:
      "The platform reserves the right to modify the terms with publication of notice of substantial updates before they take effect, and require user consent when needed.",
    termsOfUseContactTitle: "14. Contact and Legal Notices",
    termsOfUseContactContent:
      'All notices must be directed to the official contact channels listed on the "Contact Us" page and the legal address listed in the records will be accepted for official notifications.',
    howWeCollectDataTitle: "How We Collect This Data",
    howWeCollectDataContent:
      "Directly from you (registration form, service application, document uploads).\nFrom payment service providers, identity verification systems, or third parties based on your authorization.\nAutomatically (cookies, server logs).\n\nData Use and Legal Basis for Processing\nWe use data for:\nProviding services: Connecting clients with accountants, managing offers, communication, and secure payment.\nPlatform improvement: Analyzing usage to develop features, such as service recommendations.\nLegal compliance: Responding to government requests (such as the Omani Tax Authority) or PDPL.\nMarketing: Sending newsletters or customized offers, with your consent (you can withdraw at any time).\nSecurity: Detecting fraud or violations.\nFor sensitive data (such as financial records), we obtain special authorization from the competent ministry under PDPL before processing.\n\n6. Data Sharing with Third Parties\nWe do not sell your data. We only share it in the following cases:\nWith service providers: Client data with the selected accountant to provide the service, with confidentiality commitment.\nWith partners: Payment or hosting providers (such as AWS or Omani banks), with processing contracts ensuring security.\nInternational transfer: If necessary, we obtain your consent and ensure protection equivalent to PDPL (such as agreements with countries with similar laws).\nLegal entities: To comply with Omani or international laws.\nInfrastructure and cloud providers (hosting provider).\n\n7. Transfer of Data Outside the Sultanate of Oman\nIf we transfer your data outside the Sultanate (for operational needs or to use cloud services), we will implement appropriate safeguards (data transfer agreements, standard clauses, etc.) to ensure an adequate level of protection. We will ensure notification of users and allow withdrawal of consent when required by law.\n\n8. Data Retention and Retention Period\nWe retain data as long as necessary to achieve processing purposes or to comply with legal obligations (tax/commercial) or until users request deletion, taking into account compliance exceptions. We mention standard time examples (e.g., financial records 7 years or according to local legal requirements).\n\n9. User Rights\nYou have the following rights, which can be exercised via [form link or email]:\nAccess: Obtain a copy of your data.\nRectification: Correct inaccurate data.\nDeletion: Request deletion of data (we may retain some for legal purposes).\nObjection: Refuse processing for marketing purposes.\nPortability: Transfer data to another platform.\nWithdrawal: Withdraw consent at any time without compensation.\nWe respond to requests within 30 days. For sensitive data, we apply additional procedures.\n\n10. Security and Data Protection\nSecurity: We use TLS encryption, firewalls, and periodic testing to prevent unauthorized access. We appoint a DPO for oversight.\nRetention: We retain data for the period necessary for the purpose (e.g., 7 years for financial records under Omani law), then delete it securely.\nViolations: In case of a violation, we notify the ministry within 72 hours, and users if damage is likely.\n\n11. Data Breach Notification\nIn case of a data breach that may expose individuals' rights and freedoms or cause serious harm: We will notify the competent authority (Ministry/Regulatory Authority) within the time period specified by law (e.g., 72 hours from our knowledge of the incident) and we will notify affected individuals if necessary, with details of the incident and mitigation measures.\n\n12. Cookie Policy\nWe use functional cookies to improve performance and analytical cookies to understand usage. Users can adjust cookie preferences through browser settings or through the cookie portal on the website.\n\n13. Children\nWe do not target users under the age of [18] and do not intentionally collect data about minors. If we become aware of minor data, we will take immediate deletion measures.\n\n14. Changes to Privacy Policy\nWe reserve the right to modify this policy. We will publish the new version and effective date and notify users as appropriate (e.g., substantial changes require explicit consent).\n\n15. How to Contact Us or File a Complaint\n[Contact details, data protection email address, data subject rights request form]. If the complaint is not resolved internally, users have the right to approach the competent Omani data regulatory authority.",

